## What changed
Assembled the code-under-test integration branch `ta-testing` off upstream/main `11d70a8a` using `git merge --no-ff` (Dean's chosen mechanic, preserves per-PR commit provenance). DCO-signed merge commits.

- **C merge `1904306c`** — `git merge --no-ff ta-model-level-demand` (PR C #1480, model-level decode demand; source tip `25f09a87`). Clean auto-merge.
- **D merge `db530eed` (= integration HEAD)** — `git merge --no-ff ta-veto-liveness` (PR D #1481, per-analyzer liveness scale-down veto; source tip `b3f75650`). Textually auto-merged with no reported conflicts, but a **semantic** conflict surfaced at `go vet`: C had added an `arrivalRate float64` parameter to `runAnalyzersAndScore`, and D's new whole-file test `engine_v2_liveness_test.go` (no textual conflict → not flagged by git) called the pre-C signature. Resolved by adding the trailing `arrivalRate=0` argument to all 6 call sites in that test; fix folded into the D merge commit and documented in its message. No production-code change beyond the two parents.

